<title>AUSTRALIA: Burns Philp jumps after restructure news.</title>
<headline>Burns Philp jumps after restructure news.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in troubled food group Burns Philp and Co Ltd jumped 2.7 percent to A$1.90 on Monday after the company announced a restructure of its operations and a third quarter net loss of A$24.4 million.</p>
<p>The company said it was to sell its herb and spice business to focus on its yeast activities. Burns Philp also announced managing director Ian Clack would retire.</p>
</text>
